From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0404-black-world-05-upscale-own-handles-only.patch

Source: 0404-black-world-05-upscale-own-handles-only.patch
its own store, nothing else (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY)

Run81 (T23, Handheld, Max Resolution, trace): the gameplay network (first HMMA at 0xc00) reads
one image, cbuf0+0xc0 = 0x8113971000 1920x1080 E5B9G9R9 (format 32), and stores one, +0xd0 =
0x81252ff000 1920x1080 B10G11R11 (format 33). No other handle. Without a same-size rule the
stand-in found no pair in them, fell to the cbuf0 scan and blitted a 256x256 image onto a
512x512 one (131.7 s), later a 64x36 onto a 128x72 one (193.6 s): the speckled 8-pixel cells and
blurred limbs of the test clip, while the real output stayed unwritten and the world black.

EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY=1: a program whose own read and store are one size is copied from
that read to that store, E5B9G9R9 through the existing source-format override into B10G11R11,
and never takes another image of the input's size, the Bananza slots or the cbuf0 scan. A
dispatch where its own handles form no pair is skipped (logged "own handles form no pair,
nothing copied" in the trace). Programs whose own pair upscales, the movies' last pass, keep the
old path. Same-size own pairs are allowed with the switch, so EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE is not
needed beside it.

Against SAME_SIZE alone: the copy is the same (r@0xc0 -> w@0xd0, 32 -> 33); the difference is
what happens on a dispatch where the own pair is not readable: SAME_SIZE falls back to the scans
and blits unrelated images, this does nothing. Default off: nothing changes. Clang syntax check,
no warnings, after black-world-01..04. Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
 src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index 7364d0c455..ec4873f184 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -952,6 +952,17 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
     // found its pair (run75). Only the program's own handles may pair same-size images: in the
     // cbuf0 scans below any two same-size images of one format would do.
     static const bool same_size_ok = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SAME_SIZE") != nullptr;
+    // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY=1: a program whose own read and store handles hold images of
+    // one size (a 1:1 network: Ocarina of Time at Max Resolution reads one 1920x1080 E5B9G9R9
+    // image through cbuf0+0xc0 and stores one 1920x1080 B10G11R11 image through +0xd0, run81) is
+    // copied from its own read to its own store and nothing else: no other image of the input's
+    // size, no Bananza slots, no cbuf0 scan. Run81's scan paired a 256x256 with a 512x512 image,
+    // then a 64x36 with a 128x72 one, and blitted those while the real output stayed black. A
+    // dispatch where such a program's own handles form no pair is skipped. Programs whose own
+    // pair upscales (the movies' last pass) keep the old path. Same-size own pairs are allowed.
+    static const bool handles_only = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY") != nullptr;
+    const bool own_same_size = same_size_ok || handles_only;
+    static std::unordered_set<GPUVAddr> own_pair_programs; // 1:1 networks seen so far
     // EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_STEADY=1 (run75, Docked: that program's pair was found at 106 s and the
     // world showed, then it was lost again while the program kept being dispatched; the log has no
     // per-dispatch data): the program's own handle slots that last gave a pair are tried first on
@@ -1035,7 +1046,7 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             if (const auto it = remembered.find(program_address); it != remembered.end()) {
                 const auto from = image_at(it->second.read_slot, true);
                 const auto to = image_at(it->second.store_slot, true);
-                if (upscale_pair(from, to, false, same_size_ok)) {
+                if (upscale_pair(from, to, false, own_same_size)) {
                     input = from;
                     output = to;
                     input_slot = it->second.read_slot;
@@ -1050,7 +1061,7 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             // Same-size pairs: the drawn frame (E5B9G9R9, Ocarina of Time) first. Of the program's
             // other reads of the output's size, one of its format may be its own last output (a
             // temporal network's history): copying that would leave the output as it started.
-            if (same_size_ok) {
+            if (own_same_size) {
                 for (const u32 read : reads) {
                     const auto from = image_at(read, true);
                     if (from && from->format == Texture::TextureFormat::E5B9G9R9 &&
@@ -1066,7 +1077,7 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             for (const bool same_format : {true, false}) {
                 for (const u32 read : reads) {
                     const auto from = image_at(read, true);
-                    if (upscale_pair(from, to, same_format, same_size_ok) &&
+                    if (upscale_pair(from, to, same_format, own_same_size) &&
                         (!input || u64{from->Width()} * from->Height() > u64{input->Width()} * input->Height())) {
                         input = from;
                         output = to;
@@ -1083,6 +1094,7 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
         }
         const bool same_size_pair = input && output && input->Width() == output->Width() &&
                                     input->Height() == output->Height();
+        if (handles_only && same_size_pair) own_pair_programs.insert(program_address);
         if (same_size_pair) {
             static std::unordered_set<GPUVAddr> reported;
             if (reported.insert(program_address).second) {
@@ -1123,14 +1135,22 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
             break;
         }
     }
+    // A 1:1 network (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY) gets nothing but its own pair.
+    const bool own_guard = handles_only && own_pair_programs.contains(program_address) &&
+                           !upscale_pair(input, output, false, true);
+    if (own_guard) {
+        input.reset();
+        output.reset();
+        step = "own handles form no pair, nothing copied";
+    }
     // Donkey Kong Bananza's slots, after the program's own handles: other titles keep unrelated
     // images there.
-    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
+    if (!own_guard && !upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
         input = image(0x60);
         output = image(0x70);
         step = "Bananza slots";
     }
-    if (!upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
+    if (!own_guard && !upscale_pair(input, output, false, same_size_ok)) {
         input.reset();
         output.reset();
         step = "cbuf0 scan";
@@ -1201,7 +1221,7 @@ bool KeplerCompute::UpscaleInsteadOfNativeProgram() {
                    : std::string{"none"};
     };
     if (trace && (!input || !output)) {
-        trace_outcome(fmt::format("no pair (tic limit {}, cbuf0 size {:#x}):{}",
+        trace_outcome(fmt::format("no pair ({}; tic limit {}, cbuf0 size {:#x}):{}", step,
                                   static_cast<u32>(regs.tic.limit), cbuf.size.Value(),
                                   slots_text(false)));
     }
